# Purpose
Explains what the org brain is and how a member or agent uses it, without
service internals.

# Sanitization
Written fresh from private design and shipped code (rewrite-only): no hosts,
rings, ports, model routes, env names, repository names or org ids. Model
answers are described as an organisation setting. Since 2026-11-14 every
organisation can start its own brain (one brain per organisation, isolated
by the node's organisation); new brains match words only (no model answers).

# Gotchas
- Brain Talk remembers each member's answered private conversations for
  follow-ups (released; see the Brain Talk guide's 2026-11-24 reconciliation).
  Clear only empties the view, Forget erases them; other members never see them.
- Running-work summaries are org-wide (not filtered per viewer); the privacy
  section must keep saying so while that is true.
- Writers can only replace their own notes; note text max 2,000 characters.
- Without model answers, ask matches words, not meaning.
- Work authority (since 2026-11-25): the brain never acts on its own
  authority. It starts AI work only inside a current owner/admin mandate
  (kinds, default node, limits, expiry; covers any org node; never release
  or deploy; the run executes as the grantor; a Brain Talk ask starts it
  only for the grantor or an org owner/admin; a mandate never approves a
  draft). Changes it drafts (task create, run, raise priority, cancel,
  delete; schedule pause, delete; sprint rollover) run as the person, when they asked
  or confirm; permanent deletes wait 5 s behind Stop and need the person's
  own dashboard session; running an existing task needs their Run now.
  Never describe it
  as assigning work or changing tasks unasked.
- Isolation line must stay true: the node's organisation picks the brain.
- New organisations get a brain by default only where brains are available
  (one region today); keep the "where available" wording.

# Change History
- 2026-11-26: Replaces "does not run work" with the mandate and confirm-as-you rules; adds charter/guidance notes, ask depth and the agent tool rows, checked against the released browser and brain behaviour.
- 2026-11-14: One brain per organisation, deploy link, isolation, notes list/delete, full brain tool table.
- 2026-11-13: Created.
- 2026-11-27: org policy is on from the start (owner steward, every kind, no limits, revoke stays revoked); questions go to the org brain first (friendly agent, via brain, 4 h default). Merge at release of the default policy and friendly agent branches.

- 2026-11-26 (task_c6e8101f, org policy P4): "mandate" wording now says "org policy"; the org policy stands by default, the brain keeps it current inside the admin ceiling, suspends on steward loss. Describes branches feat/org-policy-p3-026f in gv-node-gateway, gv-org-brain and konui: publish with their release, not before.
